Feature: Tag
  One plane is [[it]]: the chaser. The chaser tags another plane when it touches it, and then
  that plane is it. The game is two minutes long. The game panel shows the time that each
  pilot is it, and the pilot with the least time wins. A plane that has just become it cannot
  tag back the plane that tagged it for 5 seconds.

  Stay in the [[arena]]: a circle with a radius of 90 m over the field in front of the
  [[pilot box]], below 60 m. Small cones mark its edge. If you fly out of the arena,
  you are it. A plane that is not in the air cannot be tagged. When a computer pilot crashes,
  it gets its plane back and throws it again.

  Expectation: A touch passes it on
    Given the game is tag
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the chaser is you
    When the pilot tags an opponent
    Then the chaser is an opponent

  Expectation: The chaser comes after you
    A computer pilot that is it chases the plane that it can catch most easily. Fly slowly
    and straight, and it catches you.
    Given the game is tag
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the chaser is an opponent
    When the chaser tags the plane
    Then the chaser is you

  Expectation: Out of the arena, you are it
    Given the game is tag
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the chaser is an opponent
    When the pilot leaves the arena
    Then the chaser is you

  Expectation: Two minutes of tag
    The game panel shows the results. The pilot who was it for the least time wins.
    Given the game is tag
    And the game clock is running
    When the clock runs out
    Then the game clock is stopped
